<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tepanecs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tepanec</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tepanecs were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a> whose state, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a>, dominated the region in the early fifteenth century. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> initially served them as tributaries and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> warriors. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> profile describes how the Tepanec succession crisis after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc</a>'s death in 1426 led to the war in which the Mexica and their allies destroyed Tepanec hegemony.</p></div>
